# --- data: tracked by DVC, never committed raw ------------------------------
# Payload paths are listed **by name**, one per line, rather than with a `data/<tier>/*`
# wildcard plus a `!*.dvc` negation, and rather than with `data/<tier>/*/`. Both of those
# shorter forms are read differently by git and by DVC's own walk: git honours the
# negation and does not treat `data/processed/` as ignored, while DVC's matcher does -
# so `dvc status` and `dvc repro` reported "no data or pipelines tracked" while a
# targeted `dvc push` worked, which is how an empty remote went unnoticed once already.
# A payload directory added later will show up in `git status` instead of vanishing
# silently, which is the safer failure.
data/raw/fa_bresler/
data/raw/flowchartseg/
data/raw/hdbpmn/
data/raw/sketch2code/
data/interim/edge_text/
data/interim/node_text/
data/interim/p13_golden/
data/interim/page_text/
data/interim/phashes.parquet
data/interim/pipeline_cache/
data/interim/primitives_detect/
data/interim/state_text/
data/processed/arrows/
data/processed/codegen/
data/processed/detect/
data/processed/fa_render/
data/processed/flowchartseg_images/
data/processed/ir/
data/processed/label_crops/
data/processed/manifest.parquet
data/processed/targets/
data/processed/text_crops/
data/features/descriptors.parquet
data/features/embeddings.npy
data/features/embeddings_index.parquet
data/features/embeddings_meta.json
data/features/embeddings_pca128.npy
data/features/handcrafted.parquet

